    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185">

                <pb facs="0274" n="190" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg190"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/3283</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Swiss Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sulzer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 127</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 13, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of January 30, 1918,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d185-f1"/> in
                    which you requested that arrangements be made to transfer the German subjects
                    now interned at Ellis Island to Hot
                    Springs, N. C.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to inform you that I submitted this matter to the
                    Secretary of Labor, from whom I have now received a reply <pb facs="0275"
                        n="191" xml:id="pg191"/> stating that the matter of transferring the enemy
                    aliens interned at Ellis Island, as well
                    as those at Gloucester City, N. J., to Hot Springs, N.C., was under
                    consideration and that he furthermore expected that the transfer would be
                    completed very soon, possibly within the next 10 days.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
